# 0. Steering file (do this first)

Kiro applies steering docs to every task in the repo. Without this, the agent will drift toward "helpful" defaults that defeat the point of the pipeline.

Create `.kiro/steering/upgrade-safety.md`:

```markdown
---
inclusion: fileMatch
fileMatchPattern: 'scripts/release/**|test/upgrade/**|releases/**'
---

# Upgrade pipeline rules

- Never loosen a verification check to make a test pass. If bytecode or
  selectors don't match, the correct outcome is a thrown error.
- Never compare bytecode with `startsWith`, a prefix match, or a
  substring check. Full equality after immutable/library masking only.
- Every function that sends a transaction must first assert chainId
  against the release manifest.
- No implicit signers. `ethers.getSigners()[0]` is forbidden outside
  chainId 31337/1337.
- Selector actions (ADD/UPDATE/REMOVE) are always derived from a diff
  against on-chain routing. Never hardcode an action for all methods.
- Errors must name the specific mismatch (which selector, which slot,
  which byte offset). No generic "verification failed".
- Do not add try/catch that swallows a verification failure.
- Do not modify the existing functions in
  scripts/audit/package-contract-upgrade-utils.js or deploy-package.js
  unless a task explicitly says to. Wrap them instead.
```

