# Task 2 — Release manifest schema and loader

**Prompt:**

> Create `scripts/release/manifest.js` and `schemas/release-manifest.schema.json`.
>
> The manifest is the single source of truth for a release. Schema fields: `schemaVersion`, `component`, `version`, `gitCommit`, `chainId`, `componentId`, `contextAddress`, `updatesRepository`, `expectedPackageAddress`, `compiler` (version, optimizer.enabled, optimizer.runs, viaIR, bytecodeHash, evmVersion), `package` (artifactPath, creationCodeHash, runtimeCodeHash, constructorArgs, libraries, immutables), `selectors` (add/update/remove, each an array of `{selector, signature}`), `migration` (required, target, calldata, reinitializerVersion), `rollback` (version, packageAddress, runtimeCodeHash, verified), `invariants` (array of `{name, call, expect}`), `criticalSlots` (array of bytes32).
>
> `manifest.js` exports `loadManifest(path)` which: reads the JSON, validates against the schema with ajv in strict mode, asserts every address is checksummed, asserts every selector matches `^0x[0-9a-f]{8}$`, asserts no selector appears in more than one of add/update/remove, and asserts `compiler.bytecodeHash === "none"`. Throw with the specific failing field. Also export `assertArtifactProvenance(manifest)` which recomputes `keccak256` of the artifact's creation bytecode, compares to `package.creationCodeHash`, checks `git rev-parse HEAD` equals `gitCommit`, and checks `git status --porcelain` is empty.
>
> Add a fixture at `releases/_fixtures/valid.json` and tests in `test/scripts/manifest.test.js` covering each rejection path.

**Done when:** valid fixture loads; each mutation of the fixture (bad checksum, uppercase selector, duplicated selector across add/remove, `bytecodeHash: "ipfs"`) throws with a message naming the field.

**Note:** the agent cannot know your real `componentId` or `updatesRepository` addresses. Fixtures only — you fill in real values.

