# Task 4 — Bytecode verification

**Prompt:**

> Create `scripts/release/bytecode.js` exporting `verifyDeployedBytecode(manifest, packageAddress)`.
>
> It must: throw if `eth_getCode` returns `0x`; throw if the artifact's `deployedBytecode.object` contains `__$` (unlinked library placeholder); mask the byte ranges listed in the artifact's `immutableReferences` to zero in **both** the expected and on-chain code before comparing; compare with full string equality, not a prefix or substring match; on mismatch report the byte offset of the first difference and 16 bytes of context from each side; on match compute `keccak256` of the on-chain code and assert it equals `manifest.package.runtimeCodeHash`, returning the hash.
>
> Tests in `test/scripts/bytecode.test.js` against a local Hardhat node: (a) deploy a contract and verify it passes; (b) deploy a different contract at the same manifest and assert it throws; (c) deploy a contract with an `immutable` and assert masking makes it pass; (d) assert a truncated-code case throws rather than passing on a prefix match.

**Done when:** case (d) throws — that's the one that proves the comparison isn't accidentally lenient.

