# Task 5 — Selector diff engine

This is the most important task. Give it its own session.

**Prompt:**

> Create `scripts/release/selectors.js`. This replaces the loop in `publishPackageUpdate` that pushes `Action.UPDATE` for every method.
>
> Export `getCurrentRouting(repo, componentId)` returning a `Map<selector, packageAddress>` read from the `UpdatesRepository`. Use the `IUpdatesRepository` ABI at `updates-repository-contracts/out/IUpdatesRepository.sol/IUpdatesRepository.json` — read it and use the actual method names; do not invent them. If no method exists to enumerate current routing for a component, stop and report that instead of guessing.
>
> Export `computeSelectorDiff(manifest, packageAddress)` which performs, in order, and throws on any failure:
> 1. Derive the selector set from the artifact ABI.
> 2. Read `getPackageMethods()` from the deployed package and assert it equals the ABI set. The current code trusts this call as the source of truth; here it is a value being checked.
> 3. Assert `manifest.selectors.add ∪ manifest.selectors.update` equals the ABI set.
> 4. Build `methods[]` and `actions[]`: selectors absent from current routing get `Action.ADD`, present ones get `Action.UPDATE`, and `manifest.selectors.remove` entries get `Action.REMOVE` after asserting each is currently registered.
> 5. Orphan check: any selector currently routing to `manifest.rollback.packageAddress` that appears in neither `methods[]` nor the remove list is an orphan — throw and list them.
> 6. Return `{ methods, actions, plan }` where `plan` is a human-readable array of `{selector, signature, action, from, to}`.
>
> Also export `assertNoCollisions(repo, componentId, selectors, packageAddress)` which throws if any intended selector is currently owned by a package that is neither the target nor its declared predecessor.
>
> Tests in `test/scripts/selectors.test.js` with a mocked routing map: pure addition, pure update, mixed add+update+remove, an orphaned selector, a removal of an unregistered selector, an ABI/`getPackageMethods()` disagreement, and a collision with a sibling package. Every failure case must throw with the offending selector named.

**Done when:** the orphan test and the ABI-disagreement test both throw. Those two are the defects in the current code.

