# Task 7 — State snapshot and post-upgrade verification

**Prompt:**

> Create `scripts/release/snapshot.js` exporting `captureState(manifest, contextAddress)` and `compareState(before, after, manifest, expectedPackageAddress)`.
>
> `captureState` returns `{block, values, routing, rawSlots}`: `values` from calling each `manifest.invariants[].call` as a view; `routing` from `getCurrentRouting`; `rawSlots` from `eth_getStorageAt` for each entry in `manifest.criticalSlots`.
>
> `compareState` collects **all** failures before throwing (do not throw on the first). It must check: every invariant marked `preserved` is unchanged; every invariant with a literal expectation matches; every selector in add/update routes to `expectedPackageAddress`; every selector in remove is gone from routing; every raw slot is unchanged; and — importantly — that no selector outside the declared change set changed its routing at all. Label that last case `UNEXPECTED CHANGE`.
>
> Tests in `test/scripts/snapshot.test.js` using hand-built before/after objects, one test per failure category, plus one where an undeclared selector moved.

**Done when:** the `UNEXPECTED CHANGE` test throws. That's the check that catches accidentally upgrading an extra function, which nothing currently does.

