## Sequencing

Run 1 → 2 → 3 in one sitting; they're small and everything else depends on them. Then 4, 5, 7 (the three verification primitives) — give task 5 a fresh session, it's the meatiest. Then 8 and 9 to wire them together. 10, 11, 12 can go in any order after that. 6 is independent and can be slotted anywhere. 13 last.

One thing to watch: Kiro will be tempted to make failing checks pass. The steering file addresses this, but when you review each task, the question to ask is "did it weaken an assertion to get green?" — particularly on tasks 4, 5, and 12.
